  E'A junior at a multi-strat shop trains a random forest on a two-feature direction classifier and reports 70% out-of-sample accuracy. The PM is sceptical — a real edge that strong would put the desk out of work. A code review finds the bug: `train_test_split` defaults to `shuffle=True`, so the test set is randomly drawn from across the full timeline. Future rows leak into the training fold. With chronological splitting the score collapses back to noise. Find the missing keyword.',
