  E'**Concept.** `sklearn.model_selection.train_test_split(..., shuffle=True)` — the SILENT DEFAULT — randomly samples test rows from anywhere in the array. For tabular i.i.d. data that''s correct. For time series it''s lookahead leakage by definition: the model sees rows after the test points during training. Fix: pass `shuffle=False` to keep the last `test_size` fraction as the chronological holdout. Same trap whether you''re using linear regression, gradient-boosted trees, or a neural net.\n\n**Find the bug.** `train_test_split` is silently shuffling. Add `shuffle=False` so the test set is the last 20% chronologically.\n\n**Expected.** All tests pass.',
